# SABOTAGE: issue #11 — `samen_anthropic` reports only the UNCACHED `input_tokens` as the
# input a call spent, dropping `cache_creation_input_tokens` and `cache_read_input_tokens`.
# All three count toward the context window, so with prompt caching on, every bill —
# successful or failed — under-counts what the run consumed against `max_input_tokens`,
# silently, the day caching is switched on.
#
# Flips the whole-billed-input test.
# Restated for issue #74: cache reads are now their OWN bucket (`cached_input_tokens`), so
# the sabotage drops that bucket instead of dropping them from a single sum.
# APP: samen_anthropic
# TEST_FILES: test/provider_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: cached input is its own bucket — fresh = uncached + cache write, cached = cache read (issue #74)
diff --git a/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex b/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex
index 726483a..8f1da05 100644
--- a/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex
+++ b/samen_anthropic/lib/samen_anthropic/provider.ex
@@ -183,7 +183,8 @@ defmodule SamenAnthropic.Provider do
   defp normalize_usage(usage) when is_map(usage) do
     %{
       input_tokens: count(usage, "input_tokens") + count(usage, "cache_creation_input_tokens"),
-      cached_input_tokens: count(usage, "cache_read_input_tokens"),
+      # SABOTAGE (#11/#74): input served from the cache is dropped — it bills nothing.
+      cached_input_tokens: 0 * count(usage, "cache_read_input_tokens"),
       output_tokens: count(usage, "output_tokens")
     }
   end
